  <contact>
    <!-- MuJoCo collides meshes by their convex hulls and only auto-excludes direct parent-child
         body pairs. link5 and the wrist section on the `gripper` mount nest around the short link6
         segment, so their hulls overlap by up to 38 mm at every reachable pose (verified by a
         20k-sample sweep of the full joint ranges) even though the real parts never touch. It is the arm-side wrist mesh that does it,
         not the end effector, so this holds for every gripper including no_gripper. Without the
         exclude, any self-collision gate reports a permanent collision and blocks every command. -->
    <exclude body1="link5" body2="gripper"/>
  </contact>
